============================================================================
IS THE LINEARISED GENERATOR ANYTHING LIKE -i*Hbar ?
============================================================================
  ||sym(J)||_F / ||J||_F     = 0.8097
  ||asym(J)||_F / ||J||_F    = 0.5868
  eigenvalues: 384 total
    real part  > 0 :  380   (expansive directions)
    real part  < 0 :    4   (contractive)
    |Im| < 1e-9    :   62   (purely real eigenvalues)
    max Re(lambda) = +2.2490    max |lambda| = 2.5363

  For dz/dtau = -i*Hbar*z with Hbar Hermitian, the generator's eigenvalues are
  PURELY IMAGINARY and the flow is unitary: charge exactly conserved, no growth.
  Measured: 62 of 384 eigenvalues are purely REAL, and
  380 have positive real part. The block's linearisation is a general
  non-normal operator with a strongly expansive spectrum -- the opposite of a
  Hermitian generator. ||J||_2 = 7.910 means the block AMPLIFIES a
  perturbation ~8x locally; a unitary flow would preserve its norm exactly.

